{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch481TFTNpWy86EEUs1NU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `scripts/export_invoices.py` and committed it along with `out/invoices.csv`.\n\n**The script drops segment C invoices, the same way the customers export drops segment C customers.** The commit that added the customers filter explains why: segment C customers declined partner sharing, and the contract covers every record held on them, not just the customers table. Invoices have the same `seg` column, so exporting them unfiltered would have sent the partner data it shouldn't get. Of the 12 invoices, 9 were written and 3 were left out, and the output has no segment C rows.\n\nOtherwise the script is a copy of the customers export with the file paths changed.\n\nThe commit message starts with `export_invoices:`, following the earlier script commit, rather than a month. The month prefix is for commits under `data/`, and the nightly import reloads whichever month a message starts with.\n\nAs you asked, January was left as it is: `data/2026-01.csv` is still uncommitted, and the bad row is unchanged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":320,"cache_read_input_tokens":19119,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":320},"output_tokens":316,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-62>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T04:58:06.418Z","request_id":"req_011Ch481SxMCJBykRcRr9eKc"}
